          #HomotopyTheoreticVersionOfCohomologyFunctorDefIsEquivalent.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p The three definitions
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  def.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedGeneralizedCohomology"}
              %li
                %p
                  def.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedGeneralizedCohomologyHomotopyTheoretically"}
              %li
                %p
                  def.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedGeneralizedCohomologyHomotopyHomotopicalFunctor"}
            %p are indeed equivalent.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Regarding the equivalence of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedGeneralizedCohomology"}
              with def.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedGeneralizedCohomologyHomotopyTheoretically"}
            %p
              By the existence of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#TopQuillenModelStructure"}> thm.
              ), the characterization of its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy category
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#HomotopyCategoryOfSubcategoriesOfModelCategoriesOnGoodObjects"}> cor.
              ) and the existence of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-approximations"} CW-approximations
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedGeneralizedCohomology"}
              is equivalent to the functor passing to the classical pointed homotopy category. In view of this and since on CW-complexes the standard topological mapping cone construction is a model for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofiber"} homotopy cofiber
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#StandardTopologicalMappingConeIsHomotopyCofiber"}> prop.
              ), this gives the equivalence of the two versions of the exactness axiom.
            %p
              Regarding the equivalence of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedGeneralizedCohomologyHomotopyTheoretically"}
              with def.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedGeneralizedCohomologyHomotopyHomotopicalFunctor"}
            %p
              This is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+category"} classical homotopy category
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#UniversalPropertyOfHomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory"}> thm.
              ) which identifies it with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#HomotopyCategoryOfACategoryWithWeakEquivalences"}> def.
              ) of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\ast/}
              at the weak homotopy equivalences (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#TopQuillenModelStructure"}> thm.
              ), together with the existence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+approximations"} CW approximations
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#EveryTopologicalSpaceWeaklyEquivalentToACWComplex"}> rmk.
              ): jointly this says that, up to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde F
              in the following diagram (which is filled by a natural isomorphism itself):
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Top
                              %mi op
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi F
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Ab
                              %mi ℤ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi γ
                                    %mi Top
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mover
                                  %mi F
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ho
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Top
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi op
                            %mo ≃
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Top
                              %mi CW
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Top^{op} &amp;\overset{F}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Ab^{\mathbb{Z}}
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\gamma_{Top}}}\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\tilde F}}
                    \\\
                    Ho(Top)^{op}\simeq (Top_{CW})/_\sim
                    }
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              sends weak homotopy equivalences to isomorphisms and where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_\sim
              means identifying homotopic maps.
          %p
            Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyTheoreticVersionOfCohomologyFunctorDefIsEquivalent"}
            naturally suggests (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#LurieHigherAlgebra"} Lurie 10, section 1.4
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
          #GeneralizedCohomologyOnGeneralInfinityCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ModelCategory"}> def.
              ) with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/}
              its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+model+structure"} pointed model category
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#ModelStructureOnSliceCategory"}> prop.
              ).
            %p
              A
              %strong
                reduced additive
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized cohomology theory
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mo •
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi Ho
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi op
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msup
                          %mi Ab
                          %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\tilde E^\bullet \;\colon \; Ho(\mathcal{C}^{\ast/})^{op} \longrightarrow Ab^{\mathbb{Z}}
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
                  (“
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+isomorphisms"}> suspension isomorphisms
                  ”) of degree +1
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mo •
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msup
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\sigma \; \colon \; \tilde E^\bullet \longrightarrow \tilde E^{\bullet+1} \circ \Sigma
            %p such that
            %ul
              %li
                %strong (exactness)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E^\bullet
                takes
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofiber+sequences"} homotopy cofiber sequences
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequences"} exact sequences
          %p Finally we need the following terminology:
          #AdditiveOrdinary.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E^\bullet
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+cohomology+theory"} reduced cohomology theory
              according to either of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedGeneralizedCohomology"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedGeneralizedCohomologyHomotopyTheoretically"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedGeneralizedCohomologyHomotopyHomotopicalFunctor"}
              or def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralizedCohomologyOnGeneralInfinityCategory"}
            %p
              We say
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E^\bullet
              is
              %strong additive
              if in addition
            %ul
              %li#WedgeAxiom
                %p
                  %strong
                    (
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+axiom"}> wedge axiom
                    )
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{X_i\}_{i \in I}
                  any set of pointed CW-complexes, then the canonical morphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mo ∨
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msup
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\tilde E^\bullet(\vee_{i \in I} X_i)
                        \\longrightarrow
                        \\prod_{i \in I} \tilde E^\bullet(X_i)
                %p
                  from the functor applied to their
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
                  (
                  %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#WedgeSumAsCoproduct"}> def.
                  ), to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
                  of its values on the wedge summands, is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %p
              We say
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E^\bullet
              is
              %strong ordinary
              if its value on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^0
              is concentrated in degree 0:
            %ul
              %li
                %strong (Dimension)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mover
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo ≠
                            %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E^{\bullet\neq 0}(\mathbb{S}^0) \simeq 0
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E^\bullet
              is not ordinary, one also says that it is
              %strong generalized
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %strong extraordinary
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
                of reduced cohomology theories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta \;\colon\; \tilde E^\bullet \longrightarrow \tilde F^\bullet
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              between the underlying functors which is compatible with the suspension isomorphisms in that all the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} squares commute
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mover
                                %mi E
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mover
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mi F
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mover
                                %mi E
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mrow
                                %mo •
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi Σ
                                    %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mover
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mrow
                                %mo •
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\tilde E^\bullet(X) &amp;\overset{\eta_X}{\longrightarrow}&amp;  \tilde F^\bullet(X)
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\sigma_E}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\sigma_F}}
                    \\\
                    \\tilde E^{\bullet + 1}(\Sigma X)
                    \&amp;\overset{\eta_{\Sigma X}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\tilde F^{\bullet + 1}(\Sigma X)
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p We now discuss some constructions and consequences implied by the concept of reduced cohomology theories:
          #ConnectinHomomorphismForCohomologyTheoryOnInfinityCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              Given a generalized cohomology theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mi δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E^\bullet,\delta)
              on some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              as in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralizedCohomologyOnGeneralInfinityCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofiber+sequence"} homotopy cofiber sequence
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#LongFiberSequence"}> prop.
              ),
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi f
                    %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi g
                    %mi Z
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi coker
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \stackrel{f}{\longrightarrow} Y \stackrel{g}{\longrightarrow} Z
                    \\stackrel{coker(g)}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\Sigma X
                    \\,,
            %p
              then the corresponding
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connecting+homomorphism"} connecting homomorphism
              is the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi σ
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo ˜
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi coker
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo ˜
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\widetilde E^\bullet(X)
                    \\stackrel{\sigma}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\widetilde E^{\bullet+1}(\Sigma X)
                    \\stackrel{coker(g)^\ast}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\widetilde E^{\bullet+1}(Z)
                    \\,.
          #LongExactSequenceOfACohomologyTheoryOnAnInfinityCategory.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connecting+homomorphisms"} connecting homomorphisms
              of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConnectinHomomorphismForCohomologyTheoryOnInfinityCategory"}
              are parts of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequences"} long exact sequences
              (the
              = succeed "):" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequences+in+generalized+cohomology"} long exact sequences in generalized cohomology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ∂
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ∂
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo ˜
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots
                    \\stackrel{\partial}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\widetilde E^{\bullet}(Z)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\widetilde E^\bullet(Y)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\widetilde  E^\bullet(X)
                    \\stackrel{\partial}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\widetilde  E^{\bullet+1}(Z)
                    \\to \cdots
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              By the defining exactness of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mover
                          %mi E
                          %mo ˜
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde  E^\bullet
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralizedCohomologyOnGeneralInfinityCategory"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConnectinHomomorphismForCohomologyTheoryOnInfinityCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              is by definition an isomorphism.
          %h4#unreduced_cohomology Unreduced cohomology
          %p
            Given a reduced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            as in def.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedGeneralizedCohomology"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            simply by evaluating it on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_+
            (
            %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#BasePointAdjoined"}> def.
            ). It is conventional to further generalize to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cohomology"} relative cohomology
            and evaluate on unpointed subspace inclusions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon A \hookrightarrow X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cones"} mapping cones
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cone
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cone(i_+)
            (
            %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#UnreducedMappingConeAsReducedConeOfBasedPointAdjoined"}> prop.
            ).
          %p
            In the following a
            %em pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,U)
            refers to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
            inclusion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \hookrightarrow X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \emptyset)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Top
                    %mi CW
                    %mo ↪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{CW}^{\hookrightarrow}
            for the category of such pairs (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi CW
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{CW}
            on the inclusions). We identify
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi CW
                  %mo ↪
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Top
                    %mi CW
                    %mo ↪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{CW} \hookrightarrow Top_{CW}^{\hookrightarrow}
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto (X,\emptyset)
          #GeneralizedCohomologyTheory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
              (unreduced,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cohomology"} relative
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mo •
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Top
                          %mi CW
                          %mo ↪
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi op
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi Ab
                          %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        E^\bullet : (Top_{CW}^{\hookrightarrow})^{op} \to Ab^{\mathbb{Z}}
                %p
                  to the category of
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℤ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+abelian+groups"} graded abelian groups
              %li#ConnectingHomomorphismOfUnreducedCohomology
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                  of degree +1, to be called the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connecting+homomorphism"} connecting homomorphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ∅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\delta_{(X,A)}
                        \\;\colon\;
                        E^\bullet(A, \emptyset) \to E^{\bullet + 1}(X, A)
                        \\,.
            %p such that:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %strong (homotopy invariance)
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon (X_1,A_1) \to (X_2,A_2)
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
                  of pairs, then
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        E^\bullet(f)
                        \\;\colon\;
                        E^\bullet(X_2,A_2) \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} E^\bullet(X_1,A_1)
                %p
                  is an
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %li#ExactnessUnreduced
                %p
                  %strong (exactness)
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
                  the induced sequence
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi δ
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi ⋯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\cdots
                        \\to
                        E^n(X, A)
                        \\longrightarrow
                        E^n(X)
                        \\longrightarrow
                        E^n(A)
                        \\stackrel{\delta}{\longrightarrow}
                        E^{n+1}(X, A)
                        \\to
                        \\cdots
                %p
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence"} long exact sequence
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
              %li
                %p
                  %strong
                    (
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excision"}> excision
                    )
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi A
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \hookrightarrow A \hookrightarrow X
                  such that
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mover
                            %mi U
                            %mo ¯
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi Int
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{U} \subset Int(A)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo −
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo −
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↪
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon (X-U, A-U) \hookrightarrow (X, A)
                  induces an isomorphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo −
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo −
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        E^\bullet(i)
                        \\;\colon\;
                        E^n(X, A)
                        \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                        E^n(X-U, A-U)
            %p
              We say
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
              is
              %strong additive
              if it takes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
              to
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            %ul
              %li#UnreducedAdditivity
                %p
                  %strong (additivity)
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, A) = \coprod_i (X_i, A_i)
                  is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mo ≃
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                          %mi i
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        E^n(X, A) \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} \prod_i E^n(X_i, A_i)
                %p
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                  from the value on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,A)
                  to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
                  of values on the summands.
            %p
              We say
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
              is
              %strong ordinary
              if its value on the point is concentrated in degree 0
            %ul
              %li
                %strong> (Dimension)
                \:
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo ≠
                            %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo *
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ∅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^{\bullet \neq 0}(\ast,\emptyset) = 0
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of unreduced cohomology theories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta \;\colon\; E^\bullet \longrightarrow F^\bullet
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              of the underlying functors that is compatible with the connecting homomorphisms, hence such that all these
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} squares commute
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi E
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ∅
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi A
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi ∅
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi F
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ∅
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi δ
                                    %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi δ
                                    %mi F
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi E
                              %mrow
                                %mo •
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi X
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi A
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi F
                              %mrow
                                %mo •
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    E^\bullet(A,\emptyset) &amp;\overset{\eta_{(A,\emptyset)}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; F^\bullet(A,\emptyset)
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\delta_E}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\delta_F}}
                    \\\
                    E^{\bullet +1}(X,A)
                    \&amp;\overset{\eta_{(X,A)}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    F^{\bullet +1}(X,A)
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#AguilarGitlerPrieto02"}> AGP 02, def. 12.1.1
            ).
          #AlternativeFormulationOfExcisionAxiom.num_defn
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              The excision axiom in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralizedCohomologyTheory"}
              is equivalent to the following statement:
            %p
              For all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B \hookrightarrow X
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo =
                      %mi Int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi Int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = Int(A) \cup Int(B)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i \colon (A, A \cap B) \longrightarrow (X,B)
            %p induces an isomorphism,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i^\ast
                    \\;\colon\;
                    E^\bullet(X, B)
                    \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    E^\bullet(A, A \cap B)
          %p
            (e.g
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Switzer75"} Switzer 75, 7.2
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              In one direction, suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
              satisfies the original excision axiom. Given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi Int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \Int(A) \cup Int(B)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \coloneqq X-A
              and observe that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi U
                              %mo ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mo −
                                %mi A
                              %mo ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi X
                            %mo −
                            %mi Int
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⊂
                            %mi Int
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\overline{U}
                    \&amp; = \overline{X-A}
                    \\\ &amp; = X- Int(A)
                    \\\ &amp; \subset Int(B)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p and that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (X-U, B-U) = (A, A \cap B)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence the excision axiom implies
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet(X, B) \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} E^\bullet(A, A \cap B)
            %p
              Conversely, suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
              satisfies the alternative condition. Given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \hookrightarrow A \hookrightarrow X
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi U
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{U} \subset Int(A)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Int
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo −
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∪
                            %mi Int
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo −
                            %mover
                              %mi U
                              %mo ¯
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∩
                            %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Int
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⊃
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo −
                            %mi Int
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∩
                            %mi Int
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    Int(X-U) \cup Int(A)
                    \&amp; = (X - \overline{U}) \cap \Int(A)
                    \\\ &amp; \supset (X - Int(A)) \cap Int(A)
                    \\\ &amp; = X
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p and that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (X-U, (X-U) \cap A) = (X-U, A - U)
                    \\,.
            %p Hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^\bullet(X-U,A-U)
                    \\simeq
                    E^\bullet(X-U, (X-U)\cap A)
                    \\simeq
                    E^\bullet(X,A)
                    \\,.
          %p
            The following lemma shows that the dependence in pairs of spaces in a generalized cohomology theory is really a stand-in for evaluation on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofibers"} homotopy cofibers
            of inclusions.
          #EvaluationOfCohomologyTheoryOnGoodPairIsEvaluationOnQuotient.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
              be an cohomology theory, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralizedCohomologyTheory"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^\bullet(X,A)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    E^\bullet(X \cup Cone(A), \ast)
            %p
              between the value of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
              on the pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,A)
              and its value on the unreduced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cone"} mapping cone
              of the inclusion (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#UnreducedCone"}> rmk.
              ), relative to a basepoint.
            %p
              If moreover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
              is (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
              of) a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+cell+complex"} relative cell complex
              inclusion, then also the morphism in cohomology induced from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \;\colon\; (X,A)\longrightarrow (X/A, \ast)
              is an
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^\bullet(p)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    E^\bullet(X/A,\ast)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    E^\bullet(X,A)
                    \\,.
          %p
            (e.g
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#AguilarGitlerPrieto02"} AGP 02, corollary 12.1.10
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              Consider
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ≔
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Cone
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi Cone
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \coloneqq (Cone(A)-A \times \{0\}) \hookrightarrow Cone(A)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              minus the base
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ( X\cup Cone(A)-U, Cone(A)-U) \simeq (X,A)
            %p and hence the first isomorphism in the statement is given by the excision axiom followed by homotopy invariance (along the contraction of the cone to the point).
            %p
              Next consider the quotient of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cone"} mapping cone
              of the inclusion:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ( X\cup Cone(A), Cone(A) ) \longrightarrow (X/A,\ast)
                    \\,.
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
              is a cofibration, then this is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cone(A)
              is contractible and since by the dual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+lemma"} factorization lemma
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#FactorizationLemma"}> lem.
              ) and by the invariance of homotopy fibers under weak equivalences (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#FiberOfFibrationIsCompatibleWithWeakEquivalences"}> lem.
              ),
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \cup Cone(A)\to X/A
              is a weak homotopy equivalence, hence, by the universal property of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+category"} classical homotopy category
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#UniversalPropertyOfHomotopyCategoryOfAModelCategory"}> thm.
              ) a homotopy equivalence on CW-complexes.
            %p Hence now we get a composite isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^\bullet(X/A,\ast)
                    \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    E^\bullet( X\cup Cone(A), Cone(A) )
                    \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    E^\bullet(X,A)
                    \\,.
          #GeneralizedCohomologyOnHomotopyQuotientMaps.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              As an important special case of : Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,x)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon (Cone(X), X) \to (\Sigma X,\{x\})
              the quotient map from the reduced cone on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+suspension"} reduced suspension
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^\bullet(p)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    E^\bullet(Cone(X),X)
                    \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    E^\bullet(\Sigma X, \{x\})
            %p is an isomorphism.
          #ExactSequenceOfATriple.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (exact sequence of a triple)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
              an unreduced generalized cohomology theory, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralizedCohomologyTheory"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Z \hookrightarrow Y \hookrightarrow X
            %p
              induces a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence"} long exact sequence
              of cohomology groups of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mover
                        %mi δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots
                    \\to
                    E^{q-1}(Y,Z)
                    \\stackrel{\bar \delta}{\longrightarrow}
                    E^q(X,Y)
                    \\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}
                    E^q(X,Z)
                    \\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}
                    E^q(Y,Z)
                    \\to
                    \\cdots
            %p where
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi δ
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\bar \delta
                    \\;\colon \;
                    E^{q-1}(Y,Z)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    E^{q-1}(Y)
                    \\stackrel{\delta}{\longrightarrow}
                    E^{q}(X,Y)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              Apply the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+lemma"} braid lemma
              to the interlocking long exact sequences of the three pairs
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,Y)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,Z)
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,Z)
            %p
              %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BraidDiagramForHomologyOnTripled.jpg", :width => "500"}/
            %p
              (graphics from
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://math.stackexchange.com/a/1180681/58526"} this Maths.SE comment
            %p
              See
              %a{:href => "braid+lemma#ExactSequenceForTripleInGeneralizedHomology"} here
              for details.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The exact sequence of a triple in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExactSequenceOfATriple"}
              is what gives rise to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan-Eilenberg+spectral+sequence"} Cartan-Eilenberg spectral sequence
              for
              = succeed "-cohomology" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          #ExtractingSuspensionIsomorphismFromUnreducedCohomology.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,x)
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed topological space
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cone(X) = (X \wedge (I_+))/X
              its reduced
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Cone
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\{x\}, X, Cone(X))
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExactSequenceOfATriple"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mover
                        %mi δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0
                    \\simeq
                    E^q(Cone(X), \{x\})
                    \\longrightarrow
                    E^q(X,\{x\})
                    \\overset{\bar \delta}{\longrightarrow}
                    E^{q+1}(Cone(X),X)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    E^{q+1}(Cone(X), \{x\})
                    \\simeq 0
            %p
              exhibits the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connecting+homomorphism"} connecting homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar \delta
              here as an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Cone
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\bar \delta
                    \\;\colon\;
                    E^q(X,\{x\})
                    \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    E^{q+1}(Cone(X),X)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+isomorphism"} suspension isomorphism
              extracted from the unreduced cohomology theory, see def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FromUnreducedToReducedCohomology"}
              below.
          #MayerVietorisSequenceInGeneralizedCohomology.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mayer-Vietoris+sequence"}> Mayer-Vietoris sequence
                )
            %p
              Given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
              an unreduced cohomology theory, def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralizedCohomologyTheory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interior"} interior
              of two spaces as
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo =
                      %mi Int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi Int
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = Int(A) \cup Int(B)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \subset A \cap B
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence"} long exact sequence
              of cohomology groups of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mover
                        %mi δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
