                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_0
              is the identity element in degree 0 (being a unit of an ordinary ring, by definition) and hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_n
              is necessarily its image under the suspension isomorphism, due to compatibility with the structure maps and using the above analysis.
          %h4#complex_projective_space Complex projective space
          %p
            For the fine detail of the discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theories"} complex oriented cohomology theories
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ComplexOrientatioon"} below
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+space"} complex projective space
          %p
            Complex projective space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^n
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+space"} projective space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔸
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}P^n
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔸
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A} = \mathbb{C}
            being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            (and for
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            of complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            (real dimension
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
