          %h2#ComplexOrientedCohomologyTheory Complex oriented cohomology
          %p
            %strong Idea.
            Given the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation in generalized cohomology
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#OrientationAndFiberIntegration"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theories"} cohomology theories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            such that there exists an
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+class"} Thom class
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+vector+bundle"} universal vector bundle
            over any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G
            (or rather: on its induced
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+fibration"} spherical fibration
            %em all
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            inherit an orientation.
          %p
            Considering this for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = U(n)
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+groups"} unitary groups
            yields the concept of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
          %p
            It turns out that a complex orientation on a generalized cohomology theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            in this sense is already given by demanding that there is a suitable generalization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundles"} complex line bundles
            in
            = succeed "-cohomology." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/splitting+principle"} splitting principle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+Chern+classes"} generalized Chern classes
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conner-Floyd+Chern+classes"}> Conner-Floyd Chern classes
            ) of all degrees, and these are the required universal generalized
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+classes"} Thom classes
          %p
            Where the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            is simply additive under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundles"} complex line bundles
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group+laws"} formal group laws
          %p
            %strong Literature.
            (
            %a{:href => "#Kochman96"}> Kochman 96, section 4.3
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie10"} Lurie 10, lectures 1-10
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Adams74"} Adams 74, Part I, Part II
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Pedrotti16"} Pedrotti 16
          %h3#ChernClasses Chern classes
          %p
            %strong> Idea
            \. In particular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HR"} HR
            is canonically a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conner-Floyd+Chern+classes"} Conner-Floyd Chern classes
            to be discussed
            %a{:href => "#ConnerFloydChernClasses"} below
            follows closely the behaviour of the ordinary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+classes"} Chern classes
          %p
            An ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+class"} Chern class
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
            of
            = succeed "," do
