              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Spectra
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Spectra)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi M
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi n
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi c
                                    %mi n
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^{2n}
                    \&amp;\overset{}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    M U_{2n}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{c_n}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; E_{2n}
                    }
            %p
              commutes up to homotopy, hence that the restriction of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_n
              to a fiber is the
              = succeed "-fold" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2n
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{2n}
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ThomClassesCFClass"}
            %p
              Hence componentwise all these triangles commute up to some homotopy. Now we invoke the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Milnor+sequence"} Milnor sequence
              for generalized cohomology of spectra (prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CohomologyOfSpectraMilnorSequence"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tower"} tower
              of abelian groups
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \mapsto E^{n_1}(S^n)
              is actually constant (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+isomorphism"}> suspension isomorphism
              ) hence trivially satisfies the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mittag-Leffler+condition"} Mittag-Leffler condition
              and so a homotopy of morphisms of spectra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S} \to E
              exists as soon as there are componentwise homotopies (cor.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WithSomeLefflerTheHomsOfSpectraAreHomotopicIfComponentsAre"}
            %p Next, the respect for the product demands that the square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi M
                            %mi U
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi M
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi c
                                %mo ∧
                                %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi E
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi M
                            %mi U
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    M U \wedge M U
                    \&amp;\overset{c \wedge c}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    E \wedge E
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    M U
                    \&amp;\underset{c}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    E
                    }
            %p
              commutes in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Spectra
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Spectra)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi OrthSpec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi stable
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(OrthSpec(Top_{cg}))_{stable}
              of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+orthogonal+spectra"} model structure on orthogonal spectra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#SequentialSpectraQuillenEquivalence"}> thm.
              ).
            %p
              Here the derived
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
              is given by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#SsymModuleSymmetricSpectra"}> def.
              ) and maps out of such a product are equivalently as in the above diagram is equivalent (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#DayConvolutionViaNaturalIsosInvolvingExternalTensorAndTensor"}> cor.
              ) to a suitably equivariant collection diagrams of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi M
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi M
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi c
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi n
                                      %mn 1
                                %mo ∧
                                %msub
                                  %mi c
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi n
                                      %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo ∧
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi M
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo +
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi c
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %msub
                                      %mi n
                                      %mn 1
                                    %mo +
                                    %msub
                                      %mi n
                                      %mn 2
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo +
                                %msub
                                  %mi n
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    M U_{2 n_1} \wedge M U_{2 n_2}
                    \&amp;\overset{c_{n_1} \wedge c_{n_2}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    E_{2 n_1} \wedge E_{2 n_2}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    M U_{2(n_1 + n_2)}
                    \&amp;\underset{c_{(n_1 + n_2)}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    E_{2 (n_1 + n_2)}
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where on the left we have the standard pairing operations for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M U
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#OrthogonalComplexThomSpectrum"}> def.
              ) and on the right we have the given pairing on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %p
              That this indeed commutes up to homotopy is the Whitney sum formula for Chern classes (
              %a{:href => "Chern+class#WhitneySumChernClasses"}> prop.
              ).
            %p
              Hence again we have componentwise homotopies. And again the relevant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mittag-Leffler+condition"} Mittag-Leffler condition
              on
              = succeed "-holds," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ↦
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi MU
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi MU
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \mapsto E^{n-1}((MU \wedge MU)_n)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conner-Floyd+classes"} Conner-Floyd classes
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConnerFloyedClasses"}
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WithSomeLefflerTheHomsOfSpectraAreHomotopicIfComponentsAre"}
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_6 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+commutative+ring+spectrum"} homotopy commutative ring spectrum
              (
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#HomotopyCommutativeRingSpectrum"}> def.
              ). Then the map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mi U
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi c
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi M
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (M U \overset{c}{\longrightarrow} E)
                    \\;\mapsto\;
                    (B U(1) \simeq M U_{2} \overset{c_1}{\longrightarrow} E_2)
            %p
              which sends a homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+commutative+ring+spectra"} homotopy commutative ring spectra
              to its component map in degree 2, interpreted as a class on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(1)
              via lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalComplexLineBundleThomSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              from homotopy classes of homomorphisms of homotopy commutative ring spectra to complex orientations (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StrictComplexOrientation"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie10"}> Lurie 10, lecture 6, theorem 8
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_43 Proof
            %p
              By lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#S2SpectrumMapFromComplexOrientation"}
              and lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HRingSpectrumS2SpectrumMapFromComplexOrientation"}
              the map is surjective, hence it only remains to show that it is injective.
            %p
              So let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi M
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c, c' \colon M U \to E
              be two morphisms of homotopy commutative ring spectra that have the same restriction, up to homotopy, to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi M
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi B
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1 \simeq c_1'\colon M U_2 \simeq B U(1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi M
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_n, c'_n \colon M U_{2n} \to E_{2 n}
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mo ∧
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(1)^{\wedge^n}
              is a product of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi c
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1 \simeq c'_1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_n
              becomes homotopic to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_n'
              after this restriction. But by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/splitting+principle"} splitting principle
              this restriction is injective on cohomology classes, hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_n
              itself ist already homotopic to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %msub
                        %mo ′
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c'_n
            %p It remains to see that these homotopies may be chosen compatibly such as to form a single homotopy of maps of spectra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi M
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo +
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \;\colon\; M U \wedge I_+ \longrightarrow E
                    \\,,
            %p
              This follows due to the existence of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Milnor+exact+sequence"} Milnor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
              from prop.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CohomologyOfSpectraMilnorSequence"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟵
                      %mi n
                      %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                    %mi M
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟵
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                    %mi M
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0
                    \\to
                    \\underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}^1_n E^{-1}( \Sigma^{-2n} M U_{2n} )
                    \\longrightarrow
                    E^0(M U)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}_n E^0( \Sigma^{-2n} M U_{2n} )
                    \\to
                    0
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mittag-Leffler+condition"} Mittag-Leffler condition
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MittagLefflerCondition"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConnerFloyedClasses"}
              and lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalComplexVectorBundleThomSpace"}
              all relevant maps are epimorphisms, hence the condition is satisfied by example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MittagLefflerSatisfiedInParticularForTowerOfSurjections"}
              = succeed "-term" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lim%5E1"} lim^1
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Lim1VanihesUnderMittagLeffler"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟵
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                    %mi M
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^0(M U)
                    \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}_n E^0( \Sigma^{-2n} M U_{2n} )
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M U \to E
              are equal precisely already if all their component morphisms are homotopic (represent the same cohomology class).
          %h3#HomologyOfMU
            Homology of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M U
          %p
            %strong Idea.
            Since, by the above, every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is indeed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} oriented
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundles"} complex vector bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+isomorphism"} Thom isomorphism
            which reduces the computation of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+of+MU"} homology of MU
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\bullet(M U)
            to that of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+coefficient+theorem"} universal coefficient theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kronecker+pairing"} Kronecker pairing
            and the induced duality of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Hirzebruch+spectral+sequences"} Atiyah-Hirzebruch spectral sequences
            (prop.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AHSSPairing"}
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ConnerFloydChernClasses"} above
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+homomorphism"} Hurewicz homomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman+homomorphism"} Boardman homomorphism
            the homology of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M U
            gives a first approximation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MU"} MU
          %p
            %strong Literature.
            (
            %a{:href => "#Kochman96"}> Kochman 96, section 2.4, 4.3
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie10"} Lurie 10, lecture 7
          %h3#QuillenTheoremOnMU
            Milnor-Quillen theorem on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M U
          %p
            %strong Idea.
            From the computation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+of+MU"} homology of MU
            %a{:href => "#HomologyOfMU"} above
            and applying the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman+homomorphism"} Boardman homomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi MU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet(MU)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MU"} MU
            are finitely generated. This implies that it is suffient to compute them over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+integers"} p-adic integers
            for all primes
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/change+of+rings+theorem"} change of rings theorem
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔽
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\mathbb{F}_p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequence"} Adams spectral sequence
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MU
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lazard%27s+theorem"} Lazard's theorem
            shows that there is an isomorphism of rings
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \simeq \pi_\bullet(M U)
            with the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lazard+ring"} Lazard ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen%27s+theorem+on+MU"} Quillen's theorem on MU
            says that this isomorphism is exhibited by the universal ring homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \longrightarrow \pi_\bullet(M U)
            which classifies the universal complex orientation on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M U
          %p
            %strong Literature.
            (
            %a{:href => "#Kochman96"}> Kochman 96, section 4.4
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie10"} Lurie 10, lecture 10
          %h3#landweber_exact_functor_theorem Landweber exact functor theorem
          %p
            %strong Idea.
            By the above, every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
            induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group+law"} formal group law
            from its first
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conner-Floyd+Chern+class"} Conner-Floyd Chern class
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen%27s+theorem+on+MU"} Quillen's theorem on MU
            together with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lazard%27s+theorem"} Lazard's theorem
            say that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+ring"} cohomology ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet(M U)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+cobordism+cohomology"} complex cobordism cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MU"} MU
            is the classifying ring for formal group laws.
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Landweber+exact+functor+theorem"} Landweber exact functor theorem
            says that, conversely, forming the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+cobordism+cohomology+theory"} complex cobordism cohomology theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MU"}> MU
            ) with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Landweber+exactness"} Landweber exact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            via some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group+law"} formal group law
            yields a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
          %p
            %strong Literature.
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie10"}> Lurie 10, lectures 15,16
            )
          %h2#outlook_geometry_of_
            Outlook: Geometry of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi MU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(MU)
          %p
            The grand conclusion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen%27s+theorem+on+MU"} Quillen's theorem on MU
            (
            %a{:href => "#QuillenTheoremOnMU"}> above
            ):
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
            is essentially the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+geometry"} spectral geometry
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(M U)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+formal+groups"} moduli stack of formal groups
            (1-dimensional commutative).
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Landweber-Novikov+theorem"} Landweber-Novikov theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams-Quillen+theorem"} Adams-Quillen theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams-Novikov+spectral+sequence"} Adams-Novikov spectral sequence
          %p (…)
          %p
            %strong Literature.
            (
            %a{:href => "#Kochman96"}> Kochman 96, sections 4.5-4.7 and section 5
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie10"} Lurie 10, lectures 12-14
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %hr/
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h2#References References
          %p We follow in outline the textbook
          %ul
            %li#Kochman96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Kochman"}> Stanley Kochman
              , chapters I - IV of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bordism%2C+Stable+Homotopy+and+Adams+Spectral+Sequences"} Bordism, Stable Homotopy and Adams Spectral Sequences
          %p
            For some basics in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            see also
          %ul
            %li#Switzer75
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Switzer"}> Robert Switzer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic Topology - Homotopy and Homology
          %p
            Specifically for
            %strong S.1) Generalized cohomology
            a neat account is in:
          %ul
            %li#AguilarGitlerPrieto02
              Marcelo Aguilar,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Gitler"} Samuel Gitler
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic topology from a homotopical viewpoint
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://tocs.ulb.tu-darmstadt.de/106999419.pdf"} toc pdf
          %p
            For
            %strong S.2) Cobordism theory
            an efficient collection of the highlights is in
          %ul
            %li#Malkiewich11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cary+Malkiewich"}> Cary Malkiewich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Unoriented cobordism and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mi O
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M O
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.uiuc.edu/~cmalkiew/cobordism.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            except that it omits proof of the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leray-Hirsch+theorem"} Leray-Hirsch theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+spectral+sequence"} Serre spectral sequence
            and that of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+isomorphism"} Thom isomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kochman96"} Kochman 96
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#AguilarGitlerPrieto02"} Aguilar-Gitler-Prieto 02, section 11.7
          %p
            For
            %strong S.3) Complex oriented cohomology
            besides (
            %a{:href => "#Kochman96"}> Kochman 96, chapter 4
            ) have a look at
          %ul
            %li#Adams74
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+homotopy+and+generalized+homology"} Stable homotopy and generalized homology
          %p and
          %ul
            %li#Lurie10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , lectures 1-10 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chromatic+Homotopy+Theory"} Chromatic Homotopy Theory
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#Schwede12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Symmetric+spectra"} Symmetric spectra
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/~schwede/SymSpec-v3.pdf"} pdf
